# The build context is sent to the Docker daemon in full, so without this file `.env` (real API
# keys), the local virtualenv, months of logs and cdk.out all travel with every build. The
# Dockerfiles COPY specific source directories, so nothing here is needed to build the image.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Secrets and local state
.env
.env.*
*.pem
digest_state/
logs/

# Local tooling / build output
.venv
venv
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.coverage
htmlcov
cdk.out
node_modules
*.egg-info
dist
build

# Not part of the runtime image
tests/
docs/
references/
scripts/
infrastructure/
cloudflare-proxy/
.claude/
*.md
